# cp .env.example .env  and paste your key. For most scripts nothing else is needed --
# models and timeouts have defaults in src/models.py and src/llm.py.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional second key file, .env.sao10k. It holds one line in the same format,
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=<second OpenRouter key>
# for an account whose allowed providers include Cohere and Amazon Bedrock (the primary
# key's do not); some sweeps also use it to spread spend across two key caps. Like every
# .env.* except this example, it is gitignored: never commit it.
#
# A script picks its key file with DOTENV_PATH=<file> (run_selfjudge.py and
# rerun_degenerate.py: --dotenv <file>; run_arm_eval.sh: ENV_FILE=<file>). These use
# .env.sao10k by default: run_arm_eval.sh (every lane), run_judge_first.sh and
# run_deliberate.sh (some lanes), run_noise_draw.sh (command-r7b), run_llama70b_bedrock.sh,
# llama70b_post.sh and llama70b_self.sh; each checks that the file exists before billing it.
#
# A key file named with DOTENV_PATH (or --dotenv / ENV_FILE) must exist, or src/llm.py stops
# the run, and its values override any OPENROUTER_API_KEY exported in the shell. Without
# DOTENV_PATH, .env is optional and a key already exported in the shell wins over it.
